 "result": "All in `src/tessel/views.py`:\n\n1. **`VerbView`** (subclass of `View`, line 138): its `__init_subclass__` (line 165) scans the class for attributes named after HTTP verbs (`http_method_funcs`, e.g. `get`, `post`). It sets `cls.methods` to the uppercase set, e.g. `{\"GET\", \"POST\"}`, merging in any base-class `methods`.\n\n2. **`View.to_view_func(name, *class_args, **class_kwargs)`** (around line 104–135): builds the plain view function. The generated `view(**kwargs)` instantiates the class, per request by default or once if `init_every_request` is `False`, and calls `self.run_view` via `active_app.ensure_sync`. It then attaches `view_class`, `methods`, `provide_automatic_options`, and so on to the function. It also applies any `cls.decorators`.\n\n3. **Registration**: `app.attach_route_rule(\"/counter\", view_func=CounterAPI.to_view_func(\"counter\"))` uses `view_func.methods` to restrict the rule to those HTTP methods.\n\n4. **`VerbView.run_view(**kwargs)`** (line 182): does the per-request routing. It runs `getattr(self, request.method.lower())`, falls back to `get` for `HEAD` when no `head` handler exists, and asserts a handler was found. It then calls the handler with the URL kwargs.",
